nodecode-mpp is a rewrite of tempoxyz's tempoxyz/hermes-mpp:

  https://github.com/tempoxyz/hermes-mpp
  commit a0782b7024ad0256cceede338754b466ded1df06
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Tempo (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the payment-aware HTTP path and the mpp_fetch tool, in Common Lisp
against the Nodecode cell contract. The original patches httpx inside the host
process, so every exchange in Hermes — including clients the plugin never sees
— answers challenges; a cell has no such seam, so here the same behaviour
lives in the one tool the model calls (mpp_fetch) and in /mpp: the request,
the `WWW-Authenticate: Payment` parsing (auth-params, base64url request JSON),
the origin allowlist, the response shape (status, url, headers, body,
truncated), the withholding of sensitive response headers, the body ceiling,
and one paid retry with the credential in `Authorization`.

Left out, and why: the wallet cryptography. The original signs a Tempo charge
transaction (a type-0x76 TempoTransaction with an expiring nonce, built and
signed by the pympp library); that is not reimplemented here, so the signature
comes from a payer command the section names, which may be a script over pympp
or any MPP client. Also left out: the global httpx instrumentation of traffic
other than mpp_fetch, the ledger that serializes and fails closed on duplicate
or uncertain attempts across one process, cookie reconciliation on the retry,
streaming responses, redirect guarding beyond the initial URL's host check, and
the plugin's own `hermes-mpp install` CLI, whose job — writing TEMPO_PRIVATE_KEY
into the host's .env — the section replaces.
